I suspect you don't have any really good spells. Magic missile gets
better as you level up; can be really deadly, especially with
reflection. Cone of cold and fireball can deal with several enemies at
once, and can deal with ones that are magic-resistant as well. At
post-Quest levels, all of these are far stronger than the
corresponding wands. Teleport Away and Taming can be really useful.
Finger of death can be used on Rodney and priests in the Sanctum. As a
wizard, if you have good luck and are at a high (>= 14) level, you can
easily write spellbooks to get spells that you don't know.

Bottom line: spells will rock far better than any weapon, even
Grayswandir. Your six feet of oak won't do much below the Castle.
Focus on AK items that will help you enhance spellcasting. Helm of
Brilliance and Gauntlets of Dexterity. Speed or jumping boots. Either
SDSM, CoMR, and any amulet you choose (magical breathing or life
saving, I'd suggest); or GDSM, AoR, and a robe for enhanced
spellcasting.

